here's what you didn't know about the  AT&amp;T commercial girl  everybody loves Lillie att's perky  enthusiastic commercial spokeswoman  based on her TV ads we know she's nerdy  and awkward a hopeless romantic and she  likes bedazzling but how much do you  actually know about the lady behind the  lily here's what you may not have known  about the a TMC commercial girl mallanna  Vayntrub this might blow your mind but  Lily's name isn't actually Lily it's  actually mallanna alexandrovna Vayntrub  Vayntrub was born in the u.s. Beck's  Soviet Socialist Republic or what's now  the Republic of Uzbekistan you know what  they say give us your tired your poor  and your huddled masses yearning to  become Hollywood pop-culture sensations  political refugee life in the USSR  wasn't exactly sunshine and rainbows for  the faint reps especially because they  face persistent religious persecution  for being Jewish in an officially  atheist country when mallanna was 2 her  family fled Uzbekistan in hopes of  finding religious freedom and political  asylum in America the process was long  and grueling with the family stranded in  both Austria and Italy for a while  luckily the Vayntrub made it to America  and settled in California which sounds  like a wonderful step up Barbie and ER  Lilly is hardly the first character  faint rub ever played in a commercial  she began acting in TV ads at five  starring in Barbie commercials to help  her family make ends meet her first big  break happened in 1995 when she landed a  guest spot on ER where she appeared  alongside stars like julianna margulies  at the precocious and precious age of a  high school dropout Vayntrub attended  Beverly Hills High School but she  dropped out as a sophomore but not  because she didn't value her education  she actually wanted to learn more  quickly Vayntrub got her GED and moved  on to the University of San Diego where  she earned a degree in communications  appropriate considering she's known for  selling AT&amp;T products UCB grad The  Upright Citizens Brigade is one of the  most famous comedy troupes in show  business Vayntrub honed her comedy chops  with the UCB joining other famous  graduates like Saturday Night Live bets  Kate McKinnon Bobby Moynihan and Horatio  Sanz to name a few she may not have made  the SNL cast yet  but her work with the UCB helps explain  her comedic timing  YouTube sensation Vayntrub has  guest-starred on shows like key &amp; peele  Californication and Silicon Valley but  before all that she rose to prominence  through a different channel on YouTube  as one of the co-creators of live prude  Girls Vayntrub was an early YouTube  sensation with each of her videos  earning hundreds of thousands of views  the channel is dormant now but if you  want a sneak peek at life before Lilly  you can still watch Vayntrub hit videos  online bonus points if you watch from an  AT&amp;T device the can't do nothing  movement Vayntrub created the can't do  nothing movement which has spurred  nearly a quarter of a million people  worldwide to use social media to help  crusade for the rights of refugees  around the globe saving the world by  using your AT&amp;T phone to record YouTube  videos of yourself helping refugees  that's just the kind of moment that  Lilly would absolutely love thanks for  watching subscribe to our YouTube  channel to see more videos like the one  you just saw and leave us a comment and  share your favorite Lilly moment
 

